issues.body:
From #114 (items 1-4, 13, 14, 49). An iPhone whose Safari area is about 402x655 opens the map at zoom 9.99; a 390x844 screen at 10.11. Below zoom 10 the rail lines are drawn from different geometry or layers, and there:
- G and B stop short of Union Station with a gap, then a stub at the ring;
- A stops short of Union Station, with a separate nub at the ring;
- W is cut in two near Auraria West; C is cut in two at I-25 / Broadway;
- the hub mark is a solid black disc instead of a ring (at 10.11 it is half faded, with ghost lines).

The opening zoom should also not land on a drawing threshold, so phones of different sizes see the same map.

Done when: at zooms 9 to 10.5 in steps of 0.25, both themes, every rail line is continuous into Union Station and the hub is a ring, at 402x655 and 390x844 opening views; a check finds a break or a filled hub at these zooms on the current build and passes on the fix.

Estimate: 60 min of agent time
